<title>USA: Apple unit shipments drop 17% to 698,000.</title>
<headline>Apple unit shipments drop 17% to 698,000.</headline>
<dateline>CUPERTINO, Calif. 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Apple Computer Inc said Wednesday unit shipments of its Macintosh personal computer fell 17 percent in the calendar second quarter to 698,000 units.</p>
<p>The company also said it is close to hiring an executive search firm to find a replacement for ousted Chairman Gilbert Amelio. Apple declined to name the firm.</p>
<p>The unit shipment decline was less than expected because of strong sales abroad and strong sales to schools in the U.S., said Apple Chief Financial Officer Fred Anderson.</p>
</text>
